\text{retain asset/data/contact}
\rightarrow
\text{more opportunity}

And now we get a genuinely useful invariant:

\boxed{
\Delta A > 0
}

Every serious action should ideally leave agency surface area larger than before—even when the immediate experiment fails.

A failed product test that gives you customer data, reusable code, supplier contacts, and a better pricing model can therefore be a positive result:

R_{\text{cash}}<0
\qquad\text{but}\qquad
\Delta A>0

That is Fail Forward Fast, now given an accounting system.

